@startuml t6c_fuselage_sequence

' Call sequence for t6c_fuselage -- companion to
' t6c_fuselage_class_diagram.puml (which shows the API shape). "Your Aero
' Model" (the caller, outside this library) drives every step. Single
' stateless call per evaluation -- no persistent per-step history, unlike
' t6c_landing_gear's 4-step friction-solve protocol.
' Preview in VS Code: open this file, press Alt+D.

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

actor "Your Aero Model\n(outside this library)" as Aero
participant "FuselageModel" as FM

note over FM
  Stateless: Sfront/Swet/FR/FRn/FRt
  cached once at construction
  (Sec.1 of model_formulas.pdf).
  Update() is a pure function of the
  AeroState passed in.
end note

== once, at startup ==
Aero -> FM : FuselageModel(geometry, tuning)
activate FM
FM -> FM : precompute Sfront, Swet(nose/cabin/tail), FR, FRn, FRt
FM --> Aero
deactivate FM

== every evaluation ==
Aero -> FM : ① Update(state)\n(V, rho, mu, mach, alpha, beta)
activate FM
FM -> FM : Re, Cf (Eq.2)
FM -> FM : CDsf, CDbase, CDupsweep (Sec.3, Roskam/Kroo Eq.6,7,9 -- closed-form)
FM -> FM : CD_fuselage = CDsf + CDbase + CDupsweep + windshield_drag_increment
FM -> FM : CM0_FR/dNose/dTail -> CM0 (Sec.5, anchored @ Eq.13)
FM -> FM : CMa_FR/dNose/dTail -> CMalpha (Sec.6, anchored @ Eq.14)
FM -> FM : CM = CM0 + CMalpha*alpha
FM -> FM : CNb_FR/dNose/dTail -> CNbeta (Sec.8, anchored @ Eq.16)
FM -> FM : CN = CNbeta*beta
FM --> Aero : Output\n(cd_fuselage, cm, cn, ...)
deactivate FM

Aero -> Aero : ② add cd_fuselage_sw into total CD\n(same axis as CDgear in t6texan2.xml);\nfold cm/cn in, or keep t6texan2.xml's\nown Cmo/Cmalpha/Cnb until CFD-calibrated

note over Aero, FM
  Drag (Sec.3) is closed-form Roskam/Kroo -- no calibration needed.
  See model_formulas.pdf Sec.11 ("Calibration workflow") for how to
  replace the trend-guessed CM0/CMalpha/CNbeta slopes with real numbers
  once CFD on an actual T-6C fuselage exists -- edit only
  t6c_fuselage_params.yaml, never this call sequence.
end note

@enduml
